# ThreatPulse

![ThreatPulse dashboard](./ThreatPulse%20Cybersecurity%20Intelligence%20Dashboard.png)

Prioritise the vulnerabilities and threats that deserve attention first, using
normalised, scored threat intelligence.

ThreatPulse is a threat-intelligence and vulnerability-prioritization application
that collects and normalizes current cyber-threat information to help cybersecurity
professionals identify which vulnerabilities and threats deserve attention first. It
brings together sources such as the CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV)
catalogue and applies prioritization and scoring so that security teams can focus on
the items most likely to matter rather than working through unfiltered feeds.
ThreatPulse is an independently developed analytical application intended to
support, not replace, professional judgement: its prioritization reflects the
sources and scoring applied at the time of viewing and is not an assessment,
certification or endorsement by CISA or any other authority. Users should validate
findings against their own vulnerability-management, threat-intelligence and risk
processes before acting on them.

Live at [threatpulse.iliadis.net](https://threatpulse.iliadis.net/). API discovery
document: [api/index.html](api/index.html).

## What is in this repository

| Path | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `frontend/` | React 19 + TypeScript + Vite dashboard. Static build, deployed next to the API, no server runtime. |
| `api/` | PHP read API (schema 1.0) plus the restricted write endpoint, and the human-readable API documentation at `api/index.html`. |
| `backend/` | Python pipeline: collect, normalise, correlate, enrich, score, quality gate, publish. Standard library only. |
| `deployment/` | Deployment checklist, origin restriction, the build-time stamping script and systemd/MySQL assets. |
| `api-tests/` | Contract suite that exercises the API against a local PHP + SQLite harness. |

## Quick start

```bash
# dashboard
cd frontend
npm ci
npm run dev            # http://localhost:5173, /api proxied to the live site
npm test               # unit tests
npm run build          # type-check, bundle, stamp the origin secret

# pipeline
cd backend
python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .   # 629 tests
python3 run_pipeline.py --dry-run            # collect and score, transmit nothing

# API contract
cd frontend
npm run verify:api     # local PHP + SQLite harness
```

## Deployment

See [deployment/DEPLOYMENT.md](deployment/DEPLOYMENT.md). The site is reachable only
through Cloudflare: both `.htaccess` files require a header the edge injects, and the
value is stamped at build time from a file that is not in git. The reasoning, the
rotation procedure and the verification matrix are in
[deployment/ORIGIN_RESTRICTION.md](deployment/ORIGIN_RESTRICTION.md).

## Data and attribution

Every ingested source is recorded with its provider, licence and attribution text in
`backend/data/attribution.json`. That register is published by the API at
`/api/cti/v1/attribution.php` and shown on the site Sources page.

The register records summaries, not legal advice. Each source remains subject to its
own current terms; verify them before relying on a source commercially.

## Security

Please report vulnerabilities privately, not in a public issue. See
[SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md).

